(2681805, 372259, 42100, '<td valign="top">Zen!?!  I dunno it looks like the bondo is at odds with the steel...yes, I feelin'' lots of tension here.  ;)</td>', 'Zen!?!  I dunno it looks like the bondo is at odds with the steel...yes, I feelin'' lots of tension here.  ;)', '2006-07-31 22:06:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681806, 372536, 58840, '<td valign="top">great job.  were you in stealth mode or what?</td>', 'great job.  were you in stealth mode or what?', '2006-07-31 22:06:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681810, 371438, 11923, '<td valign="top">I think this is a very sweet image.  There is some nice balance to it with your two models and the emotive quality is very nice.  I think the use of natural lighting was well handled and the focus looks pretty good.  I don''t get a strong sense of zen from the photo though, more a depiction of a zen-like action.  I find the rolling waves in the background to contradict the stillness or serenity the actions of your models might be helping to create as well.  I''m not sure how this looked in color, but the washed out nature of the waves is also a detraction for me, though I DO like the way it makes your models stand out.  All told I gave a 5.</td>', 'I think this is a very sweet image.  There is some nice balance to it with your two models and the emotive quality is very nice.  I think the use of natural lighting was well handled and the focus looks pretty good.  I don''t get a strong sense of zen from the photo though, more a depiction of a zen-like action.  I find the rolling waves in the background to contradict the stillness or serenity the actions of your models might be helping to create as well.  I''m not sure how this looked in color, but the washed out nature of the waves is also a detraction for me, though I DO like the way it makes your models stand out.  All told I gave a 5.', '2006-07-31 22:10:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681811, 372447, 11923, '<td valign="top">I think the essense of this is zennish with the negative space and floating flower.  I don''t however like the background color at all.  With the paleness of the flower (pale purple and white) the background feels very washed out and dirty which competes with the serenity the composition of the image is portraying.  The lighting is good, the focus looks a bit soft around the flower edges.  I gave a 5</td>', 'I think the essense of this is zennish with the negative space and floating flower.  I don''t however like the background color at all.  With the paleness of the flower (pale purple and white) the background feels very washed out and dirty which competes with the serenity the composition of the image is portraying.  The lighting is good, the focus looks a bit soft around the flower edges.  I gave a 5', '2006-07-31 22:10:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681814, 372517, 11923, '<td valign="top">I adore the brilliant colors of this rainbow.  Gorgeous.  Unfortunately, I''m not receiving a very zen vibe from the image.  I think you used the natural light very well and the focus is good, especially with the subject you chose.  I like the composition, but I''d suggest cropping off about an inch and a half so that the vegetation is in a compact corner and the rainbow acts as a bit of a balance and growing out of that corner.  Well.. it makes sense to me!  Heh.  At first I didn''t like the blandness of the background (not that there was much you could do about that) but now I think it does a suitable job as foil for the bright colors.  I gave a 5</td>', 'I adore the brilliant colors of this rainbow.  Gorgeous.  Unfortunately, I''m not receiving a very zen vibe from the image.  I think you used the natural light very well and the focus is good, especially with the subject you chose.  I like the composition, but I''d suggest cropping off about an inch and a half so that the vegetation is in a compact corner and the rainbow acts as a bit of a balance and growing out of that corner.  Well.. it makes sense to me!  Heh.  At first I didn''t like the blandness of the background (not that there was much you could do about that) but now I think it does a suitable job as foil for the bright colors.  I gave a 5', '2006-07-31 22:13:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681819, 372099, 58840, '<td valign="top">weird looking but very cool.  10!</td>', 'weird looking but very cool.  10!', '2006-07-31 22:15:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681825, 372217, 47541, '<td valign="top">7: nice colours and the rock is a good element to focus on</td>', '7: nice colours and the rock is a good element to focus on', '2006-07-31 22:17:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681826, 372423, 11923, '<td valign="top">I think this is a lovely seascape but I am not feeling very zennish about it as a viewer.  I''m not sure why either.  Perhaps its the composition.. the model is a very prominant subject of the image, maybe if there was more space and she was actually just a very small aspect and thus the relationship between her and the big big world would make for an interesting zen experience or if she were more to one side. it may also be because I don''t get an innate feeling of harmony or stillness from this image and that''s mostly because of all the detail and texture the rocks and scrubbrush provide.  I''m not sure.. I''m definitely no zen expert so I can only comment on what the image instills in me.  I hope this helps.  I gave a 5</td>', 'I think this is a lovely seascape but I am not feeling very zennish about it as a viewer.  I''m not sure why either.  Perhaps its the composition.. the model is a very prominant subject of the image, maybe if there was more space and she was actually just a very small aspect and thus the relationship between her and the big big world would make for an interesting zen experience or if she were more to one side. it may also be because I don''t get an innate feeling of harmony or stillness from this image and that''s mostly because of all the detail and texture the rocks and scrubbrush provide.  I''m not sure.. I''m definitely no zen expert so I can only comment on what the image instills in me.  I hope this helps.  I gave a 5', '2006-07-31 22:17:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681867, 370699, 11923, '<td valign="top">I love the duality and balance in this image and that speaks zen to me, in other images the riot of grass might dispell the zennish atmosphere for me but I think the duality of the two deer heads is strong enough that it overshadows the ''busy'' grass.  The focus looks great and the composition is very nice, though I wish it was trimmed just a bit along the sides.   I think the centered composition works well here because of the interesting visual the two deer heads make.  The use of natural light is nice though I do wish it were a bit brighter, as it is the image has a slightly blah tone to it that a bit more light and maybe an enriching of the greens might spruce up.  Focus looks good.  I actually think this might benefit from a simple black border too, kind of frame everything with something solid.  I''m bumping it up from a 5 to a 6.</td>', 'I love the duality and balance in this image and that speaks zen to me, in other images the riot of grass might dispell the zennish atmosphere for me but I think the duality of the two deer heads is strong enough that it overshadows the ''busy'' grass.  The focus looks great and the composition is very nice, though I wish it was trimmed just a bit along the sides.   I think the centered composition works well here because of the interesting visual the two deer heads make.  The use of natural light is nice though I do wish it were a bit brighter, as it is the image has a slightly blah tone to it that a bit more light and maybe an enriching of the greens might spruce up.  Focus looks good.  I actually think this might benefit from a simple black border too, kind of frame everything with something solid.  I''m bumping it up from a 5 to a 6.', '2006-07-31 22:30:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681880, 372531, 11923, '<td valign="top">I can find zen in the way the rocks line up and contrast the curve of the body, I also like the tones between the rock and the skin.  I don''t really like the candles.  While they help set the stage of the image in general I don''t find them to add anything to the zen and in fact I find them distracting me from the main subject of the rocks.  I would love to see this with a more balanced image of just the body with rocks on it, no towel/material on the hip and no candles on towel/material in the background.  Just black, curving skin, line of rocks and more skin.  I think the lighting is a bit too harsh for the image, maybe something a bit softer would give an added glow to the skin, or if not softer more of a fill from the lower hidden shoulder area.. I''m not sure.  The focus isn''t completely there, so if that could be a bit more clear I think it''d really make this image pop.   I really like the idea and potential of this shot and while it isn''t spot on for me, I think its very nice.  I''ve bumped it from a 5 to a 6</td>', 'I can find zen in the way the rocks line up and contrast the curve of the body, I also like the tones between the rock and the skin.  I don''t really like the candles.  While they help set the stage of the image in general I don''t find them to add anything to the zen and in fact I find them distracting me from the main subject of the rocks.  I would love to see this with a more balanced image of just the body with rocks on it, no towel/material on the hip and no candles on towel/material in the background.  Just black, curving skin, line of rocks and more skin.  I think the lighting is a bit too harsh for the image, maybe something a bit softer would give an added glow to the skin, or if not softer more of a fill from the lower hidden shoulder area.. I''m not sure.  The focus isn''t completely there, so if that could be a bit more clear I think it''d really make this image pop.   I really like the idea and potential of this shot and while it isn''t spot on for me, I think its very nice.  I''ve bumped it from a 5 to a 6', '2006-07-31 22:34:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681884, 369178, 21714, '<td valign="top">Not much I can say except this is wonderful, exciting and brilliant  photography.</td>', 'Not much I can say except this is wonderful, exciting and brilliant  photography.', '2006-07-31 22:35:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681895, 372422, 11923, '<td valign="top">I like the balance of the ''star'' below and the sun above.  I also really like the placid look of the lake.  That portion really speaks of serenity and stillness and thus aspects of zen to me.  The colors are a bit muted and in this instance I''m not sure if that helps the image.  I wish the colors, in the sky particularly were a little more vibrant, just to give the eyes something more to get lost in.   Also, though I do like the balance the star offers, the way it is so bright and contrasted to the still water makes it a bit jarring which pulls me out of the zen mood.  Overall I gave a 5</td>', 'I like the balance of the ''star'' below and the sun above.  I also really like the placid look of the lake.  That portion really speaks of serenity and stillness and thus aspects of zen to me.  The colors are a bit muted and in this instance I''m not sure if that helps the image.  I wish the colors, in the sky particularly were a little more vibrant, just to give the eyes something more to get lost in.   Also, though I do like the balance the star offers, the way it is so bright and contrasted to the still water makes it a bit jarring which pulls me out of the zen mood.  Overall I gave a 5', '2006-07-31 22:37:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681896, 372267, 21714, '<td valign="top">Calm and soothing. Beautiful photograph.</td>', 'Calm and soothing. Beautiful photograph.', '2006-07-31 22:37:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681902, 372501, 11923, '<td valign="top">Very delightful.  I like this image in general outside of a challenge mindset.  That said it definitely has zen aspects to me.  I think I understand that you wanted to depict hiding behind the brush and peeking in on the zen moment the swan creates but I find the grass being the most focused part of the image to be a bit distracting because I''m wanting to see beyond it and have the swan more in focus.  I''m not sure how that dynamic change would play out and if the grass would then become an irritant as being an out-of-focus barrier of sorts.  I like the way you handled the natural light and I think the composition is great. I am bumping this up from a 5 to a 6</td>', 'Very delightful.  I like this image in general outside of a challenge mindset.  That said it definitely has zen aspects to me.  I think I understand that you wanted to depict hiding behind the brush and peeking in on the zen moment the swan creates but I find the grass being the most focused part of the image to be a bit distracting because I''m wanting to see beyond it and have the swan more in focus.  I''m not sure how that dynamic change would play out and if the grass would then become an irritant as being an out-of-focus barrier of sorts.  I like the way you handled the natural light and I think the composition is great. I am bumping this up from a 5 to a 6', '2006-07-31 22:39:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681914, 371798, 11923, '<td valign="top">This is definitely a zen-like depiction.  The balance is very nice and I like the organic nature of the stones, they have a wonderful rounded, smooth feel.  That said, there''s a starkness to the image that doesn''t speak of zen to me, but rather a coldness, as if it is zen for challenge sake rather than an attempt to understand the inner feelings of zen.. does that make sense?  I''m not really that zen-trinsic myself, but though this has balance and minimalism and stillness it just doesn''t quite hit the zen button for me.  I think its technically nicely rendered but the feeling isn''t there.  I gave a 5.</td>', 'This is definitely a zen-like depiction.  The balance is very nice and I like the organic nature of the stones, they have a wonderful rounded, smooth feel.  That said, there''s a starkness to the image that doesn''t speak of zen to me, but rather a coldness, as if it is zen for challenge sake rather than an attempt to understand the inner feelings of zen.. does that make sense?  I''m not really that zen-trinsic myself, but though this has balance and minimalism and stillness it just doesn''t quite hit the zen button for me.  I think its technically nicely rendered but the feeling isn''t there.  I gave a 5.', '2006-07-31 22:42:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681930, 372266, 11923, '<td valign="top">I think this a wonderful portrait and for that I gave it a 5.  I think your handling of natural light is great, there are only a few hotspots on the knees, forehead and belly, none of which are enough to be distracting.  I think the position of your subject is wonderful, I can almost feel her enjoying the sunshine.  I think the detail in the sand sort of belies the zennish feeling in the image, I would''ve preferred something more blank as your background, if only a less kicked up section of sand.  I do think there are aspects of zen in the image though, she certainly looks serene and at harmony with the world though I don''t think that translates into me the viewer feeling the same way exactly.  Still I think this a well rendered image, thus the 5</td>', 'I think this a wonderful portrait and for that I gave it a 5.  I think your handling of natural light is great, there are only a few hotspots on the knees, forehead and belly, none of which are enough to be distracting.  I think the position of your subject is wonderful, I can almost feel her enjoying the sunshine.  I think the detail in the sand sort of belies the zennish feeling in the image, I would''ve preferred something more blank as your background, if only a less kicked up section of sand.  I do think there are aspects of zen in the image though, she certainly looks serene and at harmony with the world though I don''t think that translates into me the viewer feeling the same way exactly.  Still I think this a well rendered image, thus the 5', '2006-07-31 22:46:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681943, 372259, 21714, '<td valign="top">Beautiful composition with delicious tones. Knowing what it is, I am still wondering if rotating 90° CW would be worth it .. just a thought.<br/>A favourite as it is.</td>', 'Beautiful composition with delicious tones. Knowing what it is, I am still wondering if rotating 90° CW would be worth it .. just a thought.A favourite as it is.', '2006-07-31 22:49:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681950, 369739, 33361, '<td valign="top">I almost did something VERY similar to this...</td>', 'I almost did something VERY similar to this...', '2006-07-31 22:50:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2681952, 372129, 11923, '<td valign="top">Very nice, vibrant image.  I like the greens and blues (though I wish the sky were a bit less cyan).  I think there is stillness and a sense of minimalism of sorts to the image but as a viewer I''m not feeling much in the way of zen exactly.  As I look at this, I''m wondering how the image would look if she was sitting not under the tree but to the left, in that empty space, sort of acting as a balance to the tree.  Might not work but her outfit being green and white made me envision her in position over there and it seemed to work in my mind but I could also be crazy.  :)  The focus isn''t quite as sharp on the subject (girl under tree) and seems more focus on a portion of the grass.  Use of the natural light is good though!  The horizon seems a bit tilted but not extravegantly so.  I gave a 5</td>', 'Very nice, vibrant image.  I like the greens and blues (though I wish the sky were a bit less cyan).  I think there is stillness and a sense of minimalism of sorts to the image but as a viewer I''m not feeling much in the way of zen exactly.  As I look at this, I''m wondering how the image would look if she was sitting not under the tree but to the left, in that empty space, sort of acting as a balance to the tree.  Might not work but her outfit being green and white made me envision her in position over there and it seemed to work in my mind but I could also be crazy.  :)  The focus isn''t quite as sharp on the subject (girl under tree) and seems more focus on a portion of the grass.  Use of the natural light is good though!  The horizon seems a bit tilted but not extravegantly so.  I gave a 5', '2006-07-31 22:50:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2682000, 369087, 61705, '<td valign="top">Good tonal range and DoF. Interesting subject matter too. I like it a lot, 9.</td>', 'Good tonal range and DoF. Interesting subject matter too. I like it a lot, 9.', '2006-07-31 23:11:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2682032, 372394, 60698, '<td valign="top">Nice!</td>', 'Nice!', '2006-07-31 23:21:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2682046, 372274, 35444, '<td valign="top">Oh, this is just lovely.  I really like the perspective.</td>', 'Oh, this is just lovely.  I really like the perspective.', '2006-07-31 23:25:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2682049, 372000, 59415, '<td valign="top">I am torn on this one.  Great photo, I can see the Zen potential, but if I were to look at this without knowing it was a zen challenge I might not think of it as Zen.  Still it is peacefull and very well done.  I give it a 7.</td>', 'I am torn on this one.  Great photo, I can see the Zen potential, but if I were to look at this without knowing it was a zen challenge I might not think of it as Zen.  Still it is peacefull and very well done.  I give it a 7.', '2006-07-31 23:25:53.000000', NULL, 1),
