(2684101, 372549, 30049, '<td valign="top">I like this very much.  This is a valid case for a centered composition.  Works well.  I think you went a bit overboard on the blue saturation however.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I like this very much.  This is a valid case for a centered composition.  Works well.  I think you went a bit overboard on the blue saturation however.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-08-01 15:46:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2684106, 371314, 30049, '<td valign="top">Ahhh...aren''t we clever?  ;^)  Actually, it''s a pretty cool shot and should work ok for this challenge.  Title does a nice job of putting it together.  Some will probably say "don''t like the edge of the plate", etc...I think the plate edge helps give this image context.  Best of luck to you.</td>', 'Ahhh...aren''t we clever?  ;^)  Actually, it''s a pretty cool shot and should work ok for this challenge.  Title does a nice job of putting it together.  Some will probably say "don''t like the edge of the plate", etc...I think the plate edge helps give this image context.  Best of luck to you.', '2006-08-01 15:48:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2684118, 372408, 30049, '<td valign="top">...and I''ll raise you a daisy!  ;^)  Very nice floral shot.  Great DOF, nice color and exposure.  Composed quite pleasingly.  One problem (not for me, but for many voters)...it''s a flower!  ;^)  Good luck.</td>', '...and I''ll raise you a daisy!  ;^)  Very nice floral shot.  Great DOF, nice color and exposure.  Composed quite pleasingly.  One problem (not for me, but for many voters)...it''s a flower!  ;^)  Good luck.', '2006-08-01 15:50:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2684125, 371266, 30049, '<td valign="top">This almost looks surreal.  I think it''s because the sky/clouds aren''t in focus (you must have used a shallower aperture, say F11 or so?).  Not that that is a bad thing as it allows the stem and flower bud pop out a little more.  Should be ok for meeting the Zen group for this.  ;^)  Good luck.</td>', 'This almost looks surreal.  I think it''s because the sky/clouds aren''t in focus (you must have used a shallower aperture, say F11 or so?).  Not that that is a bad thing as it allows the stem and flower bud pop out a little more.  Should be ok for meeting the Zen group for this.  ;^)  Good luck.', '2006-08-01 15:52:52.000000', NULL, 1),
