(2686568, 372497, 11923, '<td valign="top">Lovely image.  I can sense zen with portions of the subject though the vegetation at the bottom seems irrelevant and not needed for the photo.  I love the use of light here, its wonderful.  I think the focus looks very good as well.  Were it my preference I would''ve cropped the image right above where that orangey hued one was, I''ve scrolled the screen to block that out and to me the resulting photo seems to emphasize not only the play of light but also that one stem that''s reaching out further than the others into the semi-darkness.  Great photo.  I gave a 6</td>', 'Lovely image.  I can sense zen with portions of the subject though the vegetation at the bottom seems irrelevant and not needed for the photo.  I love the use of light here, its wonderful.  I think the focus looks very good as well.  Were it my preference I would''ve cropped the image right above where that orangey hued one was, I''ve scrolled the screen to block that out and to me the resulting photo seems to emphasize not only the play of light but also that one stem that''s reaching out further than the others into the semi-darkness.  Great photo.  I gave a 6', '2006-08-02 02:30:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2686585, 372551, 11923, '<td valign="top">I can absolutely find the zen in this image, I like the simplicity of it and the sun streak makes a great subject.  Unfortunately, I find the technical aspects to be a bit lacking and that really effects the impact the image has.  First there is a strange tone to the colors, I''m not sure if its because of the light and how its reflecting off the water or what.  Your horizon is tilted a bit and that''s very noticeable in this image and finally the focus looks like it could be a bit sharper.   I like what you were going for and I think it certainly meets the challenge, but because of the technical issues I gave a 4.</td>', 'I can absolutely find the zen in this image, I like the simplicity of it and the sun streak makes a great subject.  Unfortunately, I find the technical aspects to be a bit lacking and that really effects the impact the image has.  First there is a strange tone to the colors, I''m not sure if its because of the light and how its reflecting off the water or what.  Your horizon is tilted a bit and that''s very noticeable in this image and finally the focus looks like it could be a bit sharper.   I like what you were going for and I think it certainly meets the challenge, but because of the technical issues I gave a 4.', '2006-08-02 02:33:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2686595, 371711, 11923, '<td valign="top">Good contrasts in texture and size.  I think the play of the small twig versus the negative space works well and bring a sense of zen.   I think the focus is a bit off though, a sharper focus would really help set the twig off from the background (which kind of makes it meld in since the colors are very similar).  The white light on a drop? or something is a bit distracting too.  Since it doesn''t seem to be an important aspect of the image (due to its out of focus nature) its brightness does draw the eye away from the leaves as a whole.   I think cropping it just a bit at the top so the dark portions were gone might help as well.  I gave a 4</td>', 'Good contrasts in texture and size.  I think the play of the small twig versus the negative space works well and bring a sense of zen.   I think the focus is a bit off though, a sharper focus would really help set the twig off from the background (which kind of makes it meld in since the colors are very similar).  The white light on a drop? or something is a bit distracting too.  Since it doesn''t seem to be an important aspect of the image (due to its out of focus nature) its brightness does draw the eye away from the leaves as a whole.   I think cropping it just a bit at the top so the dark portions were gone might help as well.  I gave a 4', '2006-08-02 02:36:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2686603, 372121, 43281, '<td valign="top">Zen photography and this theme with the plastic bags is a bit fogged to death,but<br/>still it is very good I gave a 7</td>', 'Zen photography and this theme with the plastic bags is a bit fogged to death,butstill it is very good I gave a 7', '2006-08-02 02:37:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2686607, 372126, 43281, '<td valign="top">If this isnt Zen i give up</td>', 'If this isnt Zen i give up', '2006-08-02 02:38:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2686619, 372132, 11923, '<td valign="top">This is a nice image of something zennish.  The colors are good but with so much green the subject seems to blend in almost.  I also find all the vegetation to be very busy in the background and that doesn''t bring harmony or stillness to me as a viewer.  I think if you were to have a shallower DOF that would blend the details of the bushes and trees into a nice smooth (though mottled) background that would then highlight the statue and the rock, there''d be a nice play between the softened background and the architecture of the statue as well as an interesting play between the very vertical statue and the small round rock.  Those are just my impressions though.  The use of natural light is good and I think the focus though improveable (seems more on the background trees than the foreground statuary) is still good.  I gave a 5</td>', 'This is a nice image of something zennish.  The colors are good but with so much green the subject seems to blend in almost.  I also find all the vegetation to be very busy in the background and that doesn''t bring harmony or stillness to me as a viewer.  I think if you were to have a shallower DOF that would blend the details of the bushes and trees into a nice smooth (though mottled) background that would then highlight the statue and the rock, there''d be a nice play between the softened background and the architecture of the statue as well as an interesting play between the very vertical statue and the small round rock.  Those are just my impressions though.  The use of natural light is good and I think the focus though improveable (seems more on the background trees than the foreground statuary) is still good.  I gave a 5', '2006-08-02 02:40:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2686633, 372194, 11923, '<td valign="top">Excellent.  I like the choice of the vertical negative space.  Works well with this composition.  I also like the time of day you chose since it allows the bike''s shadow to add interest to the image.  While I don''t necessarily feel anything zen when I look at the image, I do think it meets some of the aspects mentioned in the challenge description.  It is quiet, it is still and it is simple.  I do wish the focus was just a tad sharper on the entire bike (the front portion looks great), though that could just be because of the bit of shadow on the back wheel.  Anyway.  I gave a 6</td>', 'Excellent.  I like the choice of the vertical negative space.  Works well with this composition.  I also like the time of day you chose since it allows the bike''s shadow to add interest to the image.  While I don''t necessarily feel anything zen when I look at the image, I do think it meets some of the aspects mentioned in the challenge description.  It is quiet, it is still and it is simple.  I do wish the focus was just a tad sharper on the entire bike (the front portion looks great), though that could just be because of the bit of shadow on the back wheel.  Anyway.  I gave a 6', '2006-08-02 02:42:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2686640, 372547, 11923, '<td valign="top">Lovely.  Very organic and though the smoke is in a bit of a tangle I think the shapes it is creating and the nature of the subject itself lends the image to feeling free and light instead of busy/noisy.  The lighting looks great and I like the composition.  I really like how the smoke kind of has a similarity to some asian writing characters.  I think the focus is a bit soft, but working with smoke its probably hard to get tack-sharp focus.  I definitely feel the zen and I like the simple display of this image.  I gave a 7</td>', 'Lovely.  Very organic and though the smoke is in a bit of a tangle I think the shapes it is creating and the nature of the subject itself lends the image to feeling free and light instead of busy/noisy.  The lighting looks great and I like the composition.  I really like how the smoke kind of has a similarity to some asian writing characters.  I think the focus is a bit soft, but working with smoke its probably hard to get tack-sharp focus.  I definitely feel the zen and I like the simple display of this image.  I gave a 7', '2006-08-02 02:44:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2686784, 369973, 60195, '<td valign="top">Very nice... awesome detail, and great overall feel to this.  Strong entry (and a fav)  :O)</td>', 'Very nice... awesome detail, and great overall feel to this.  Strong entry (and a fav)  :O)', '2006-08-02 03:12:06.000000', NULL, 1),
