(2699384, 372267, 47816, '<td valign="top">I like the way the water bends around the leaf, photoshop technique??</td>', 'I like the way the water bends around the leaf, photoshop technique??', '2006-08-06 14:02:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699393, 370167, 29009, '<td valign="top">Good choice of subject.  Unfortunately, a number of technicals have gone slightly off.  The nose breaks the cheek line - a slightly different angle would have helped with that.  Additionally, the background bisects the frame and the subject twice, once with the water line and again with the tree line.  Overall, the image looks almost cloudy and lacks contrast.  Something has gone wrong with the facial definition - the eyelids are noticeably more lined/wrinkled that the rest of the skin and this makes it seem like too much NeatImage (or whatever) was used.  Overall, it''s a decent shot that meets the challenge, however, with all of these small nitpicky things in composition and post processing just slightly off it misses the mark a bit, for me.  Hope this helps...</td>', 'Good choice of subject.  Unfortunately, a number of technicals have gone slightly off.  The nose breaks the cheek line - a slightly different angle would have helped with that.  Additionally, the background bisects the frame and the subject twice, once with the water line and again with the tree line.  Overall, the image looks almost cloudy and lacks contrast.  Something has gone wrong with the facial definition - the eyelids are noticeably more lined/wrinkled that the rest of the skin and this makes it seem like too much NeatImage (or whatever) was used.  Overall, it''s a decent shot that meets the challenge, however, with all of these small nitpicky things in composition and post processing just slightly off it misses the mark a bit, for me.  Hope this helps...', '2006-08-06 14:11:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699395, 372080, 29009, '<td valign="top">The best of the rock shots (that I''ve seen so far, anyway).  Nice job.  :)</td>', 'The best of the rock shots (that I''ve seen so far, anyway).  Nice job.  :)', '2006-08-06 14:14:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699402, 371991, 11923, '<td valign="top">Very nice capture.  I think your handling of the natural light is good and the focus looks great to me.  Colors look a little flat, not sure if a bump in saturation would help or lead to unnatural looking effects.  I like the composition for the most part but I''d prefer to have it cropped just under the line of trees on the horizon and leave the pelican to look as if it is swiming/floating through clouds.  A bit more serene/surreal and the illusion would add another dimension to the image IMO.  I gave a 6.</td>', 'Very nice capture.  I think your handling of the natural light is good and the focus looks great to me.  Colors look a little flat, not sure if a bump in saturation would help or lead to unnatural looking effects.  I like the composition for the most part but I''d prefer to have it cropped just under the line of trees on the horizon and leave the pelican to look as if it is swiming/floating through clouds.  A bit more serene/surreal and the illusion would add another dimension to the image IMO.  I gave a 6.', '2006-08-06 14:25:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699409, 372007, 11923, '<td valign="top">Very beautiful colors here.  I like the vibrancy.  I like the balance and the negative space.  I wish the two petals at the bottom had been clipped off so it looked more like the flower was floating in unseen water (they may be reflections but if that''s the case one looks missing.  The lighting is pretty good, though I wonder if an adjustment would make the flower glow just a bit more against that black background.  Also the focus is softer than I''d expect something with such crisp lines and clear contrasts to have.  I gave a 6</td>', 'Very beautiful colors here.  I like the vibrancy.  I like the balance and the negative space.  I wish the two petals at the bottom had been clipped off so it looked more like the flower was floating in unseen water (they may be reflections but if that''s the case one looks missing.  The lighting is pretty good, though I wonder if an adjustment would make the flower glow just a bit more against that black background.  Also the focus is softer than I''d expect something with such crisp lines and clear contrasts to have.  I gave a 6', '2006-08-06 14:28:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699416, 371453, 11923, '<td valign="top">Interesting contrasts in shapes and colors.  I don''t think I understand the significance or meaning behind the choices but it is different.  I like the nice line the katana makes and the way the white candle really pops against the black background.  Unfortuantely, all of the focus seems to be on the hilt circle thingie and since both the katana AND the candle are forefront, the focus should encompass both items better IMO.  There is a bit of a flatness to the image as well, I''m not sure if alternate lighting would help by adding some sort of depth or not (with the black background adding shadows wouldn''t really work) as it looks now it just looks like a sword and candle were put down and photographed, no real sense of as to why they were paired.  But that could just be my weird way of looking at things.  Regardless, I gave a 5.</td>', 'Interesting contrasts in shapes and colors.  I don''t think I understand the significance or meaning behind the choices but it is different.  I like the nice line the katana makes and the way the white candle really pops against the black background.  Unfortuantely, all of the focus seems to be on the hilt circle thingie and since both the katana AND the candle are forefront, the focus should encompass both items better IMO.  There is a bit of a flatness to the image as well, I''m not sure if alternate lighting would help by adding some sort of depth or not (with the black background adding shadows wouldn''t really work) as it looks now it just looks like a sword and candle were put down and photographed, no real sense of as to why they were paired.  But that could just be my weird way of looking at things.  Regardless, I gave a 5.', '2006-08-06 14:32:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699419, 372480, 11923, '<td valign="top">Nice capture.  I don''t often like the images that have part of the subject blownout on white backgrounds but I think this one works.  I especially like the way the blownout right is balanced by the shadows in the back.  The rock/clay has some great details.  While I do like the negative space shown above, I wish either the crop was tighter on the left or more space was given on the left so the subject felt more cradled into the corner of the image.  I gave a 6</td>', 'Nice capture.  I don''t often like the images that have part of the subject blownout on white backgrounds but I think this one works.  I especially like the way the blownout right is balanced by the shadows in the back.  The rock/clay has some great details.  While I do like the negative space shown above, I wish either the crop was tighter on the left or more space was given on the left so the subject felt more cradled into the corner of the image.  I gave a 6', '2006-08-06 14:35:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699422, 372457, 11923, '<td valign="top">I think this is a very nice example of portraiture.  The subject is very crisp and cleanly defined from the background.  I think the pristineness (is that a word?) of her outfit really contrasts nicely with the dark, rough dirt of the rocks too.  She has a lovely smile on her face and that helps give the image a feeling of intimacy.  While I do think this is a very well done portrait technically I don''t find much in the way of Zen in it.  Zen is of course a personal thing so it''s likely to be different for everyone.  I gave a 5 for its technical merits and would''ve scored it higher if I could sense the Zen.</td>', 'I think this is a very nice example of portraiture.  The subject is very crisp and cleanly defined from the background.  I think the pristineness (is that a word?) of her outfit really contrasts nicely with the dark, rough dirt of the rocks too.  She has a lovely smile on her face and that helps give the image a feeling of intimacy.  While I do think this is a very well done portrait technically I don''t find much in the way of Zen in it.  Zen is of course a personal thing so it''s likely to be different for everyone.  I gave a 5 for its technical merits and would''ve scored it higher if I could sense the Zen.', '2006-08-06 14:38:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699424, 371798, 29009, '<td valign="top">Very nice.</td>', 'Very nice.', '2006-08-06 14:39:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699425, 372099, 11923, '<td valign="top">Ooh I like the drama in this image.  Great use of highly contrasted visuals.  The knots and turns of this branch are great and I like all the detailing the bark creates.  The lighting is great, really brings out the intricacies of the image and I can certainly find zen in this.  I think I''d rather there was space on at least one side of the subject at the bottom so it didn''t feel cramped into a small area.  I also wish the focus was just a smidge sharper throughout.  I love the title.  I gave a 7</td>', 'Ooh I like the drama in this image.  Great use of highly contrasted visuals.  The knots and turns of this branch are great and I like all the detailing the bark creates.  The lighting is great, really brings out the intricacies of the image and I can certainly find zen in this.  I think I''d rather there was space on at least one side of the subject at the bottom so it didn''t feel cramped into a small area.  I also wish the focus was just a smidge sharper throughout.  I love the title.  I gave a 7', '2006-08-06 14:41:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699435, 372523, 46601, '<td valign="top">love the composition here ... very well done</td>', 'love the composition here ... very well done', '2006-08-06 14:48:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2699436, 370693, 46288, '<td valign="top">Awesome! Meets the challenge and technically perfect. Good treatment of the light, nice composition, good job with the editing. COngratulations.</td>', 'Awesome! Meets the challenge and technically perfect. Good treatment of the light, nice composition, good job with the editing. COngratulations.', '2006-08-06 14:49:09.000000', NULL, 1),
