(2702269, 372057, 39375, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by oOWonderBreadOo:</b></div><hr/><i> it''s funny- I find this photo perfect in every way- just not zen! I mean- I didn''t vote and probably would have voted it high anyway, but wow!!! The composition spells explosion to me! Absolute energy and look at that face- just exploration on his little mind. I LOVE it!!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I guess it was so much easier for me to think of this as Zen. Picture yourself walking through this really nice, huge garden. And it''s nearly silent except for a gentle breeze and trickling water from a nearby fountain. (a Japanese fountain seen in outtake #2...<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=375946" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39375/thumb/375946.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39375/thumb/375946.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39375/thumb/375946.jpg"/></a>...) Then while walking you see this little guy''s sihlouette slowly creeping up that leaf and stop juuuust right so as to only peek his head over. Given the surroundings I was in at the time and the feel of the moment, it seemed pure Zen to me.<br/> <br/>thanks for the comment!</td>', 'Originally posted by oOWonderBreadOo: it''s funny- I find this photo perfect in every way- just not zen! I mean- I didn''t vote and probably would have voted it high anyway, but wow!!! The composition spells explosion to me! Absolute energy and look at that face- just exploration on his little mind. I LOVE it!!!   I guess it was so much easier for me to think of this as Zen. Picture yourself walking through this really nice, huge garden. And it''s nearly silent except for a gentle breeze and trickling water from a nearby fountain. (a Japanese fountain seen in outtake #2......) Then while walking you see this little guy''s sihlouette slowly creeping up that leaf and stop juuuust right so as to only peek his head over. Given the surroundings I was in at the time and the feel of the moment, it seemed pure Zen to me. thanks for the comment!', '2006-08-07 09:20:07.000000', NULL, 0),
