(2704287, 370286, 40386, '<td valign="top">Hey Jimmy I see you have the 350D Rebel now, wonderful shot, I gave it a 9 and really thought it would finish higher, definitely one of the underrated shots in this challenge.</td>', 'Hey Jimmy I see you have the 350D Rebel now, wonderful shot, I gave it a 9 and really thought it would finish higher, definitely one of the underrated shots in this challenge.', '2006-08-07 22:07:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704290, 372166, 40386, '<td valign="top">I liked this shot a lot and gave it a 9, thought it would finish higher than it did.</td>', 'I liked this shot a lot and gave it a 9, thought it would finish higher than it did.', '2006-08-07 22:09:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704373, 372285, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment:<br/> <br/>Very tranquil and lovely - the mist really adds to the quietness of this shot.  Greens are gorgeous - particularly the reflections in the water.  What makes the composition work for me is the slight reverse "S" formed by the mist and the reflection in the water - really gives a nice flow.</td>', 'Trading Post comment: Very tranquil and lovely - the mist really adds to the quietness of this shot.  Greens are gorgeous - particularly the reflections in the water.  What makes the composition work for me is the slight reverse "S" formed by the mist and the reflection in the water - really gives a nice flow.', '2006-08-07 22:39:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704383, 371981, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>Very peaceful!  I like how you got the sun with the red tint and without blowing out the whole picture.  That little bit of pink just above the sun really adds a nice touch in my opinion.  The only nit I''d have is the overall color seems a bit gray to me - not sure if you can tweak that in post processing without changing the colors you captured in the sun or not.  Composition is very good - nice execution of rule of thirds.</td>', 'Trading Post comment Very peaceful!  I like how you got the sun with the red tint and without blowing out the whole picture.  That little bit of pink just above the sun really adds a nice touch in my opinion.  The only nit I''d have is the overall color seems a bit gray to me - not sure if you can tweak that in post processing without changing the colors you captured in the sun or not.  Composition is very good - nice execution of rule of thirds.', '2006-08-07 22:43:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704393, 372463, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>I really like this.  When I first saw it in the challenge, it was one of those that made me stop and really look, because it had an interesting "feel" to it.  I do like the use of the fisheye for this - not sure it would have worked nearly as well otherwise.  To me, it is zen, and to some degree it also conveys aloneness, which is different than loneliness in that aloneness can be very peaceful and comfortable.</td>', 'Trading Post comment I really like this.  When I first saw it in the challenge, it was one of those that made me stop and really look, because it had an interesting "feel" to it.  I do like the use of the fisheye for this - not sure it would have worked nearly as well otherwise.  To me, it is zen, and to some degree it also conveys aloneness, which is different than loneliness in that aloneness can be very peaceful and comfortable.', '2006-08-07 22:47:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704447, 371981, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - Nice and simple shot here. Great gradient in the sun but overall not alot of wow factor to this (but then would alot of wow be zen?). The sky is a bit noisy. Using a noise reduction filter or even some blur to reduce that would have helped out. Mayeb tweaking the colors a bit to bring out more than the gray could have helped as well.</td>', 'Trading Post - Nice and simple shot here. Great gradient in the sun but overall not alot of wow factor to this (but then would alot of wow be zen?). The sky is a bit noisy. Using a noise reduction filter or even some blur to reduce that would have helped out. Mayeb tweaking the colors a bit to bring out more than the gray could have helped as well.', '2006-08-07 23:05:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704458, 370909, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>Well I didn''t beat you by much... but since I don''t beat you very often these days, allow me a moment to gloat...  :-)  OK, moment over.  First I must admit that I am not a huge fan of infared - I know a lot of people really like it, but to me it reminds me of flocked Christmas trees and I''ve never liked flocked Christmas trees.  Christmas trees should be green and smell of pine.  Period.  <br/> <br/>The setting and the composition (once I get past the flocked trees) is pretty peaceful (though it probably wasn''t with the kids whining and all).  Would that you could get rid of the building, though.  The one thing I will say for infared is it makes the river a lovely color.<br/> <br/>All in all, I''d take a 5.8 that you "phfftttt" at any day. <br/> <br/>Heh!  Just read Posthumous'' broku - it does look like popcorn eating the bridge...</td>', 'Trading Post comment Well I didn''t beat you by much... but since I don''t beat you very often these days, allow me a moment to gloat...  :-)  OK, moment over.  First I must admit that I am not a huge fan of infared - I know a lot of people really like it, but to me it reminds me of flocked Christmas trees and I''ve never liked flocked Christmas trees.  Christmas trees should be green and smell of pine.  Period.   The setting and the composition (once I get past the flocked trees) is pretty peaceful (though it probably wasn''t with the kids whining and all).  Would that you could get rid of the building, though.  The one thing I will say for infared is it makes the river a lovely color. All in all, I''d take a 5.8 that you "phfftttt" at any day.  Heh!  Just read Posthumous'' broku - it does look like popcorn eating the bridge...', '2006-08-07 23:12:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704468, 371566, 30982, '<td valign="top">I like the juxtaposition of the visible grass and the reflected reeds - particularly where they almost touch along the same paths.  My nit with this is that to me the green is too green.  I realize it probably IS that green, but when you live where it doesn''t rain, green this green seems artifical.</td>', 'I like the juxtaposition of the visible grass and the reflected reeds - particularly where they almost touch along the same paths.  My nit with this is that to me the green is too green.  I realize it probably IS that green, but when you live where it doesn''t rain, green this green seems artifical.', '2006-08-07 23:17:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704491, 371438, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''d have to say that the little boy joining your shoot was serendipity in addition to fine zen.</td>', 'I''d have to say that the little boy joining your shoot was serendipity in addition to fine zen.', '2006-08-07 23:27:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704499, 372034, 49865, '<td valign="top">This is a very worthy recipient of a ribbon. I''m usually not a fan of IR photography, but this really works. You''re absolutely right, this does have ''magic''.</td>', 'This is a very worthy recipient of a ribbon. I''m usually not a fan of IR photography, but this really works. You''re absolutely right, this does have ''magic''.', '2006-08-07 23:30:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704508, 372309, 49865, '<td valign="top">I like the picture a lot, but I think you should''ve used mori for the kanji representation instead (three trees arranged in a triangle instead of two side by side). My understanding is that "mori" has more the connotation of forest, and also, odd numbers of things jive better with Japanese aesthetic.</td>', 'I like the picture a lot, but I think you should''ve used mori for the kanji representation instead (three trees arranged in a triangle instead of two side by side). My understanding is that "mori" has more the connotation of forest, and also, odd numbers of things jive better with Japanese aesthetic.', '2006-08-07 23:35:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704511, 372121, 27373, '<td valign="top">I cannot believe this is a plastic bag.  When I voted on it I thought, scarf, maybe a bridal veil.  Well done.</td>', 'I cannot believe this is a plastic bag.  When I voted on it I thought, scarf, maybe a bridal veil.  Well done.', '2006-08-07 23:38:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704519, 371993, 47852, '<td valign="top">Wow... I was right about the location!  This is a beautiful shot, and not the typical angle I''ve seen shots taken from up there.  Great job!! :)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kteach:</b></div><hr/><i> Lovely colors... I like the hint of green in the bottom that keeps the entire foreground from being a total silhouette.  My first thought was that it looked like the escarpment in Thatcher Park in NY.  I''ll be back after voting to see where this was taken! :) </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Wow... I was right about the location!  This is a beautiful shot, and not the typical angle I''ve seen shots taken from up there.  Great job!! :) Originally posted by kteach: Lovely colors... I like the hint of green in the bottom that keeps the entire foreground from being a total silhouette.  My first thought was that it looked like the escarpment in Thatcher Park in NY.  I''ll be back after voting to see where this was taken! :) ', '2006-08-07 23:42:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2704529, 371566, 48228, '<td valign="top">This deserved a much higher score, and I gave you an 8. I feel there were many entries underated, so guess we just have to live with it. Thank you for your support, as it does means such a lot to me. <br/>You are definately one of my mentors, and alway take an interest in your work, as I love everything you do. <br/>I admire your ability to get on with it, and could learn a lot from you. Thanks so much mate, and tem captain.</td>', 'This deserved a much higher score, and I gave you an 8. I feel there were many entries underated, so guess we just have to live with it. Thank you for your support, as it does means such a lot to me. You are definately one of my mentors, and alway take an interest in your work, as I love everything you do. I admire your ability to get on with it, and could learn a lot from you. Thanks so much mate, and tem captain.', '2006-08-07 23:47:53.000000', NULL, 0),
