(2716392, 372519, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i>... people appreciated the technical quality but didn''t care for the subject. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>This is funny -- that''s about the opposite way my photos usually score ...<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments.</td>', 'Originally posted by DrAchoo:... people appreciated the technical quality but didn''t care for the subject.  This is funny -- that''s about the opposite way my photos usually score ... Thanks for the comments.', '2006-08-11 00:30:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2716403, 371840, 47541, '<td valign="top">I saw you were looking for comments so...<br/> <br/>I gave this a 5 in the challenge.  It got a 5 because it is a nice shot but didn''t fit what I was looking for in "zen''.  it is a bit busy.  The tree without the model and a slightly different angle to use the path as a leading line to the tree would have done it.  I also think with the model there I want to see more detail of her.  She is netiher in fully in silhouete or in detail.</td>', 'I saw you were looking for comments so... I gave this a 5 in the challenge.  It got a 5 because it is a nice shot but didn''t fit what I was looking for in "zen''.  it is a bit busy.  The tree without the model and a slightly different angle to use the path as a leading line to the tree would have done it.  I also think with the model there I want to see more detail of her.  She is netiher in fully in silhouete or in detail.', '2006-08-11 00:36:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2716476, 371898, 1031, '<td valign="top">You might try softening the shadows on the near side of the sticks just a touch-- they may add just enough excess contrast to add an element of harshness to an otherwise pastoral (and pastel) scene.</td>', 'You might try softening the shadows on the near side of the sticks just a touch-- they may add just enough excess contrast to add an element of harshness to an otherwise pastoral (and pastel) scene.', '2006-08-11 01:18:43.000000', NULL, 0),
