(2719095, 370909, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/>   The clouds and the water are fantastic! That said, I really don''t like the infrared too much. And I know it''s not fair, but I tend to vote down these types of pictures. They just look too unnatural to me. I actually didn''t vote on this one for that reason. My zen didn''t do too well, so take this with a grain of salt... it just doesn''t seem like a zen type picture. There is too much going on.</td>', 'Trading post...   The clouds and the water are fantastic! That said, I really don''t like the infrared too much. And I know it''s not fair, but I tend to vote down these types of pictures. They just look too unnatural to me. I actually didn''t vote on this one for that reason. My zen didn''t do too well, so take this with a grain of salt... it just doesn''t seem like a zen type picture. There is too much going on.', '2006-08-11 20:02:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2719113, 371812, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/>  Congrats on the 5th place! I know I said that in the thread, but wanted to put it here too. You don''t need any help with this one!</td>', 'Trading post...  Congrats on the 5th place! I know I said that in the thread, but wanted to put it here too. You don''t need any help with this one!', '2006-08-11 20:10:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2719252, 372156, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote for the Zen challenge so this is the first time I''ve taken a look at your image.  I think the comments given during the challenge give a good summary as to why your image scored where it did.  Overall the image quality is very good but I dont think the voters felt this fit the Zen description very well.  One commenter said the silence was too loud, meaning that the image is too busy and complicated.  Another thought this would fit into an architecture challenge very well.  Both are saying that this wasnt the best subject to choose for a Zen challenge.<br/> <br/>On the technical side, the lighting, composition and cropping of this image are very well done.  Ill make a couple of suggestions on what you could do different in post processing but they are based purely on my personal taste and not on any shortcomings I see in your image.  First you might want to try making the sky a little bit bluer.  Second, it would be interesting to see what a little more contrast would do for this image.  Both of these could be accomplished using a combination of levels, curves, saturation or contrast and brightness.<br/> <br/>I really like this image and Im glad it got assigned to me for review.  If you would like to discuss it further, feel free to PM me.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club I didn''t vote for the Zen challenge so this is the first time I''ve taken a look at your image.  I think the comments given during the challenge give a good summary as to why your image scored where it did.  Overall the image quality is very good but I dont think the voters felt this fit the Zen description very well.  One commenter said the silence was too loud, meaning that the image is too busy and complicated.  Another thought this would fit into an architecture challenge very well.  Both are saying that this wasnt the best subject to choose for a Zen challenge. On the technical side, the lighting, composition and cropping of this image are very well done.  Ill make a couple of suggestions on what you could do different in post processing but they are based purely on my personal taste and not on any shortcomings I see in your image.  First you might want to try making the sky a little bit bluer.  Second, it would be interesting to see what a little more contrast would do for this image.  Both of these could be accomplished using a combination of levels, curves, saturation or contrast and brightness. I really like this image and Im glad it got assigned to me for review.  If you would like to discuss it further, feel free to PM me. Tim', '2006-08-11 21:29:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2719559, 369178, 32997, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot and remember it well from the challenge..I like this kind of shot...there you are walking along and you see something that requires you to stop and process and engage your mind with...and from this simple wall you have found a genuine relationship..one that is fleeting...two shadows try to meet, but can''t quite make it work..the one on the right looks enough like a face to really make it beautifully weird...<br/> <br/></td>', 'I really like this shot and remember it well from the challenge..I like this kind of shot...there you are walking along and you see something that requires you to stop and process and engage your mind with...and from this simple wall you have found a genuine relationship..one that is fleeting...two shadows try to meet, but can''t quite make it work..the one on the right looks enough like a face to really make it beautifully weird... ', '2006-08-11 23:49:10.000000', NULL, 0),
