(2822555, 372500, 61448, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> Calm, yes, but unremarkable to me as a photograph - a bit too much empty space. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>space = calm, calm = harmony, harmony = zen... I do believe we were not talking photo here but zen (calm/harmony) Sorry you missed the point.</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: Calm, yes, but unremarkable to me as a photograph - a bit too much empty space.   space = calm, calm = harmony, harmony = zen... I do believe we were not talking photo here but zen (calm/harmony) Sorry you missed the point.', '2006-09-11 05:44:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2822560, 372500, 61448, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Shy Clicker:</b></div><hr/><i> I enjoy your sense of humour, but this might be too minimalistic for most. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>some people just have no sense of humor/zen.... I once went on a binge,,, take a pic and try to say everything with a photo what seems to show nothing... I really, really like this attempt... but I do believe many will not stop and think long enough to understand my point. You did very well... a "10" on interpretation.</td>', 'Originally posted by Shy Clicker: I enjoy your sense of humour, but this might be too minimalistic for most.   some people just have no sense of humor/zen.... I once went on a binge,,, take a pic and try to say everything with a photo what seems to show nothing... I really, really like this attempt... but I do believe many will not stop and think long enough to understand my point. You did very well... a "10" on interpretation.', '2006-09-11 05:46:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2822563, 372500, 61448, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by msgoodygal:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow, this is definately minimal.  And serene.  Just a tad bit too small to keep my interest.  A busy photo makes my eyes work too hard, disrupting the overall attempt at serenity.  Yours, although the opposite, seems to do the same thing, it forces my eye to look for what I''m missing.  Great job from the ''Great Job Baggie''! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>look for what you are missing = makes you think. Thinking makes the brain wrinkle. The more wrinkles on yer brain the more info. you are storing. Liking my pic = a very wrinkly brain. I like you.</td>', 'Originally posted by msgoodygal: Wow, this is definately minimal.  And serene.  Just a tad bit too small to keep my interest.  A busy photo makes my eyes work too hard, disrupting the overall attempt at serenity.  Yours, although the opposite, seems to do the same thing, it forces my eye to look for what I''m missing.  Great job from the ''Great Job Baggie''!   look for what you are missing = makes you think. Thinking makes the brain wrinkle. The more wrinkles on yer brain the more info. you are storing. Liking my pic = a very wrinkly brain. I like you.', '2006-09-11 05:48:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2822567, 372500, 61448, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SandyP:</b></div><hr/><i> This will probably be a fairly controversial photo as far as the voting goes.  People will either love it or hate it.  I personally like it alot!  I wish there were a few more stars in the sky, but I think it really is a beautiful depiction of silence. . .peace. . .harmony.  Good luck. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>wow.... a fan......    I took this with the hope others would see the same simple/complex idea...<br/> <br/>As for more stars... they would distract from the subject. This works just fine... deep darknes with a touch/hope of light.<br/> <br/>thank you!</td>', 'Originally posted by SandyP: This will probably be a fairly controversial photo as far as the voting goes.  People will either love it or hate it.  I personally like it alot!  I wish there were a few more stars in the sky, but I think it really is a beautiful depiction of silence. . .peace. . .harmony.  Good luck.   wow.... a fan......    I took this with the hope others would see the same simple/complex idea... As for more stars... they would distract from the subject. This works just fine... deep darknes with a touch/hope of light. thank you!', '2006-09-11 05:50:55.000000', NULL, 0),
